---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Alaa Badr — technologist, traveler, and storyteller in Seattle."
>
  <div class="max-w-content mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-22">
    <h1 class="font-playfair text-4xl font-semibold text-charcoal mb-10">About</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-charcoal leading-[1.8]">
      <p>
        I was born in Cairo, raised between Egypt and the Gulf, and have called Seattle home
        for the past fifteen years. I am a technologist by profession — you can find that side
        of me at <a href="https://alaabadr.org" class="text-terracotta hover:text-deep-terracotta transition-colors">alaabadr.org</a> — but
        this space is for everything else.
      </p>

      <p>
        I speak Arabic, English, and enough French to order dinner confidently and apologize
        for my accent afterward. I am a diver, an amateur bread baker, and someone who believes
        that the best conversations happen over long meals with nowhere to be afterward.
      </p>

      <p>
        My wife and I are raising three daughters who are, in no particular order: opinionated,
        hilarious, and better at technology than I am. They are the reason I write — partly to
        leave them something to read one day, and partly because they keep giving me things
        worth writing about.
      </p>

      <p>
        I travel whenever I can. I am drawn to places where the food is honest, the architecture
        tells a story, and the locals are willing to sit with a stranger over coffee. I have
        a particular weakness for old markets, coastal towns, and any restaurant where the menu
        is handwritten.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is my quiet page — a place to think slowly about travel, food, culture, fatherhood,
        and the small things that make a life feel full. If any of it resonates, I am glad you are here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
